Word statistics.

The word count of a sentence (text) is a whole number:
the length of the words of the sentence.

The different words in a sentence (text) is a whole number:
the length of the distinct of the words of (the sentence in lower case).

The long words in a sentence (text) is a list of texts:
each word in the words of the sentence where the length of the word is more than 4.

For example, the word count of "the kite flies high" is 4.
For example, the different words in "The cat saw the dog" is 4.
For example, the long words in "a small kite flies higher" joined with " " is "small flies higher".
